  "reason": "Round-5 follow-up to Phase 11b. Fifth shape of the same defect: prefer-get-by-test-id named getByTestId(x) as the replacement whenever the test id sat on the target compound, without checking what PRECEDED it. '#login-modal [data-testid=save]' was answered 'Use getByTestId(\"save\")', which searches the whole document -- while the identical locator written '#login-modal >> [data-testid=save]' correctly abstained since the round-3 fix, so the two spellings gave opposite answers. ALL NINE of immich's prefer-get-by-test-id findings were this ([data-viewer-content] [data-testid=ocr-box]); they are now prefer-semantic-locator info instead of a wrong warn, which is the whole of this baseline's movement. Totals are unchanged at 1973 -> 1676 (297 removals); the split moves: prefer-get-by-test-id 511 -> 502 (direct 426 -> 417), prefer-semantic-locator 1165 -> 1174. Second P1: getByTestId() resolves exactly one attribute (use.testIdAttribute, default data-testid), so suggesting it for [data-test=x] or [data-test-id=x] on a stock config named a locator that selects different elements. TestPilot now reads use.testIdAttribute from the Playwright config and qualifies the suggestion when they differ; corpus incidence is 0, which is why five rounds and a green bench missed it. Also corrected here: the has/hasText row is 253, not 252 -- it never absorbed the one removal round 4's own fix added. That is the third arithmetic correction recorded in this file rather than replaced silently.",
